.TH PATH_NUM 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
path_num \- Calculate the length of the path up to a specified component

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/path_internal.h>

.IB size_t
.IB path_num(const char* p, size_t len, int n);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBpath_num\fR function calculates the length of the path up to a specified component. It skips the first \fIn\fR components of the path and returns the length of the remaining part.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB p
The input path string.
.TP
.IB len
The length of the input path string.
.TP
.IB n
The number of components to skip.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the length of the path up to the specified component.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBpath_num\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/path_internal.h>

int main() {
    const char* path = "/usr/lib/bin";
    size_t len = path_num(path, strlen(path), 2);
    printf("Path length up to component 2: %zu\n", len);
    return 0;
}
.nef